{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Not a man is El, that He should lie.</b> In His words that He said to me — 'You shall not curse the people'; if so, how can you say, ״וקבנו לי משם״?" "<b>He has said, and will He not do it.</b> If it refers back to the Holy One, blessed be He, it would be with wonder (interrogatively); and if it returns with the language of definiteness and knowledge, it refers to a son of man, whom he mentioned as one who repents — for he says ״ולא יעשה״ and speaks and does not fulfill; but not so the Holy One, blessed be He, Who decrees and fulfills." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״לא איש אל ויכזב״ — because Balaam foresaw that a certain man (in Ishmael) was destined to lead the world astray and say that he is a prophet, he began to cry out: A man who becomes a prophet is destined to repent, and says a thing and cannot do it, as it is said: ״ההוא אמר ולא יעשה״. ״לא איש אל ויכזב״ — in good; but when He speaks to bring evil, He retracts, as it is said: ״ההוא אמר ולא יעשה״. Know this: for He said to Abraham (Genesis 15:5) ״וספור הכוכבים״, and it was fulfilled, as it is said (Deuteronomy 1:10) ״והנכם היום ככוכבי השמים״; this is ״לא איש אל ויכזב״ — in good; but in evil, ״ההוא אמר ולא יעשה״: He said to Israel (Hosea 1:9) ״כי אתם לא עמי״, then went back and said (Hosea 2:1) ״ואמרתי ללא עמי עמי אתה״ — hence you learn: ״ההוא אמר ולא יעשה״. Thus they expounded in Tanḥuma."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:30.530491873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}